    "body": "I found one more remaining \"MIME type portion\" by Ctrl+Fing: https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/mimesniff/pull/36.html#determining-the-computed-mime-type-of-a-resource step 1.\r\n\r\nLots of places return MIME types as strings instead of as structs, e.g. https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/mimesniff/pull/36.html#sniffing-a-mislabeled-binary-resource step 2-5. Probably not worth fixing now, and I'm not sure how we'd fix it eventually. (Even with struct literal notation, it'd be fairly verbose.)\r\n\r\nI'd like to work on a JS implementation of this, probably as an evolution of https://github.com/jsdom/content-type-parser. If you were able to create a JSON resource in web platform tests we could use, like for URLs, that'd be awesome.",
